## 1. NWS 事件页面：Sawyerville–Eoline Tornado – April 27, 2011

- **标题**：Sawyerville-Eoline Tornado - April 27, 2011  
- **URL**：https://www.weather.gov/bmx/event_04272011sawyerville  
- **发布方/作者**：National Weather Service (NWS) Birmingham, Alabama – Weather Forecast Office  
- **发布日期/更新日期**：页面未标明具体发布日期；内容为对 2011 年 4 月 27 日事件的官方事后测评与摘要  
- **来源类型**：美国联邦政府 / NWS 官方事件总结页面  
- **触发它的查询语句**：  
  - 原始查询："2011 Sawyerville-Eoline tornado Alabama April 27 2011 fatalities injuries affected communities National 
Weather Service"  
  - 追加查询："Sawyerville-Eoline April 27 2011 tornado database injuries fatalities Greene Hale Bibb"

### 与验收标准的相关性

1. **官方伤亡数据（fatalities / injuries）**

   页面顶部事件摘要表格中，明示字段：

   - **Injuries/Fatalities:**  
     - **“50 Injuries / 7 Fatalities”**（原文格式：`****50 Injuries / 7 Fatalities****`）

   该字段直接给出了这条 EF-3 龙卷风的总官方伤亡人数。

2. **主要受影响社区 / 区域**

   同一页面中，“National Weather Service meteorologists surveyed ...” 
段落详细描述了路径和受灾地点。关键内容（保持原意，略去部分非关键词）如下（加粗为关键地点）：

   - 开始位置与早期路径：

     > “The tornado touched down in far southwest **Greene County** near the **Tombigbee River** just west of 
**Tishabee** on County Road 69 near Head Drive, and headed northeast across rural Greene County north of **Forkland**. 
At least 4 mobile homes, 3 outbuildings, and 2 churches were damaged or destroyed along with numerous trees. Two minor 
injuries were noted in Greene County. The track started as an EF-1 but increased to an EF-2 rating while in Greene 
County.”

   - 穿越 Black Warrior River 至 Hale County、Saw yerville 及周边：

     > “The tornado crossed the **Black Warrior River** and into **Hale County** west of **Sawyerville**. The tornado 
crossed AL Route 14, just north of **Sawyerville**, where it intensified to an EF-3 rating with winds of 145 mph. As the
tornado continued northeast, it crossed **CR 18**, **CR 21**, **AL Hwy 69 south of Harper Hill**, and **CR 29 east of 
Ingram**. Extensive structural damage was noted in these locations, which resulted in at least 40 injuries and 6 
fatalities. Numerous mobile homes and single family homes and one church were damaged or destroyed. Thousands of trees 
were knocked down. The tornado moved into the **Talladega National Forest** near **Ingram**, where it caused significant
tree damage to the Bibb County line.”

   - 穿入 Bibb County，经过 Eoline 及周边，直至终止：

     > “The tornado tracked northeastward where it caused significant tree damage in the **national forest**. The 
tornado moved through **Eoline** and caused significant structural damage consistent with an EF-3 rating and winds of 
145 mph. Numerous mobile homes and single family homes sustained minor to major damage. A dozen mobile homes and single 
family homes were destroyed. In addition, the **Eoline Fire Dept** and another business were destroyed. One fatality 
occurred in a vehicle near the fire dept. At least 10 other injuries were noted. The tornado continued northeast and 
crossed **AL Hwy 5**, south of **West Blocton** where it weakened slightly to an EF-2 with winds of 125 mph. Several 
mobile homes and single family homes sustained major damage or were destroyed near **CR 26**. Along the path, thousands 
of trees were downed. The tornado continued to weaken and lifted just northeast of **Marvel**.”

   由此可知，该官方页面明确列出了主要受影响的社区、道路和区域，包括（但不限于）：

   - 县级：  
     - Greene County  
     - Hale County  
     - Bibb County（包括 Talladega National Forest 一带）

   - 具体社区 / 地名：  
     - Tishabee（Greene County，Tombigbee River 以西区域）  
     - Forkland（Greene County 北部附近的农村区域）  
     - Sawyerville（Hale County；AL Route 14 附近）  
     - Harper Hill（AL Hwy 69 南部一带）  
     - Ingram（Talladega National Forest 近 Bibb County）  
     - Eoline（Bibb County；含 Eoline Fire Dept）  
     - West Blocton 以南（AL Hwy 5）  
     - Marvel 附近（终止点东北）

   - 重要设施 / 基础设施：  
     - Eoline Fire Department（被毁）  
     - “another business” near Eoline Fire Dept（被毁）

   此内容满足“官方来源识别主要受影响社区”的验收标准。

