among many others, describe coordinated emergency medical response and public-safety actions across the state but 
generally treat the Sawyerville–Eoline tornado as part of the aggregate of storms rather than as a separate case 
study.[11] In these sources, local emergency services, hospitals, and public-health agencies are reported to have 
