central and eastern United States.[6][8] Outbreak overviews from Grokipedia and Tornado Talk describe a multi-day 
sequence of severe thunderstorms and tornadoes from 25 to 28 April 2011, with 27 April representing the single most 
active and deadly day of the event.[6][8] Both sources identify Alabama as one of the states hardest hit by strong and 
violent tornadoes on 27 April, with numerous long-track tornadoes causing widespread destruction and hundreds of 
