summary statistics differ slightly. Grokipedia reports that the outbreak produced about 362 tornadoes in total, whereas 
the Tornado Talk overview gives a figure of about 368 tornadoes, reflecting differences in data sources or counting 
methodology.[6][8] For 27 April specifically, Grokipedia cites approximately 199 tornadoes, while Tornado Talk estimates
about 224 tornadoes for that day.[6][8] The two sources also report slightly different overall fatality totals, with 
Grokipedia giving about 321 deaths associated with the outbreak and Tornado Talk listing about 324 fatalities.[6][8] 
Despite these minor discrepancies, both accounts consistently portray the outbreak as one of the most significant 
tornado events in U.S. history and emphasize the major role of Alabama tornadoes, including the Sawyerville–Eoline 
storm, in contributing to the high casualty and damage figures.[6][8][9]\n\nThe NWS Birmingham outbreak summary for 27 
