cites approximately 199 tornadoes, while Tornado Talk estimates about 224 tornadoes for that day.[6][8] The two sources 
also report slightly different overall fatality totals, with Grokipedia giving about 321 deaths associated with the 
outbreak and Tornado Talk listing about 324 fatalities.[6][8] Despite these minor discrepancies, both accounts 
consistently portray the outbreak as one of the most significant tornado events in U.S. history and emphasize the major 
